      "title": "Career Center & Services",
      "description": "Career Center & Services – Pacific States University (323) 731-2383 admissions@psuca.edu Schedule of Classes Transcript Request PSU E-mail Populi Portal Our University About PSU History Mission & Objectives PSU Identity Accreditation and Licensing Leadership Board of Trustees President University Personnel Directory University Faculty Directory Statistics PSU Disclosures Admissions Overview Admission Requirements Degree Specifics International Students Transferring Students Students with Special Circumstances Accounting Certificate Program Admission Requirement Application Apply Now Application Deadline Net Price Calculator Finance Financial Policies Tuition and Other Fees Payment Method Academic Programs College of Business Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) Master of Business Administration (MBA) College of Computer Science Bachelor of Science (BS) Master of Science (MS) Continuing Education Center Accounting Certificate Program Office of Registrar Register for Classes Add / Drop / Swap Official Transcript Request Resources Academic Calendar Academic Policies Download Forms Jobs Opportunities Catalog Units conversion chart Campus Life Student Life You Are In, What’s Next? Student Services Facilities Career Services Student Housing Disability Services International Student Guide International Office Curricular Practical Training (CPT) Optional Practical Training (OPT) OPT STEM Extension Resources Student Rights and Responsibilities On-Campus Jobs Opportunities Scholarship Opportunities Download Forms Cyber Learning Center Commencement 2026 Research The Buffinger & Evans Research Institute (J1) PSU AI & Robotics Excellence Lab PSU Student Publication FAQ ✕ Career Center & Services Home Career Center & Services PSU Career Center (E227) contains books on job searching, creating resumes, writing cover letters and interviewing skills. PSU’s Career Services (E219) provides one-on-one counseling, small group workshops, networking events, career and job listings as well as materials to assist students in their career investigations and endeavors. Employment and career advising is also available via appointments. Quarterly workshops include Resume / Curriculum Vitae creation and refinement, cover letter development, and other job search strategies. Mock interviews are available for students who want to practice and refine their skills. Networking events will be scheduled to assist students with connecting with the leaders in the various industries in Southern California. Clarify Your Goals Polish Your Job Search Skills Find Job Opportunities Research Employers & Salaries Job Listings Reporting Requirements PSU requires all graduates to update their personal information and employment information to Student & Career Services. If you are employed, you are required to submit a copy of your job offer letter and report employment information . The information must be reported to Student & Career Services during the 1st year of completion of the program within 10 days of any changes. Report Change of Personal Information Report Employment Information Employer Survey Contact Us Career Services careerservices@psuca.edu Career Center & Services Clarify Your Goals Polish Your Job Search Skills Research Employers & Salaries Find Job Opportunities Job Listings Optional Practical Training (OPT) OPT STEM Extension About Us Pacific States University is a private non-profit educational institution approved to operate by the Bureau for Private Postsecondary Education (BPPE) and accredited by the Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges (ACCSC). Popular Links Academic Catalog Tuition and Other Fees Download Forms Academic Calendar PSU on Facebook Alumni Our Address Pacific States University 3530 Wilshire Boulevard, Suite 1110 Los Angeles, CA 90010 Tel: (323) 731-2383 501(c)(3) Nonprofit, Pacific States University | Terms of Use | All Rights Reserved Need Help? Chat with us Start a Conversation Hi! Click one of 