    "http://www.accsc.org/": {
      "title": "Ensuring",
      "description": "Homepage - ACCSC Skip to content Search Accredited Schools Contact Us Standards of accreditation About About As an accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education, ACCSC has continually demonstrated that it is a valid and reliable authority on the assessment of education quality. Learn More Mission & Core Values ACCSC's mission is to ensure quality education that enhances student success in the workforce. Commissioners ACCSC‘s Board of Directors. Leadership team Supporting the Accrediting Commission's strategic vision to enhance the student educational experience and student achievement outcomes. CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Explore our career opportunities and join our team. STAFF DIRECTORY Contact our staff. SCHOOL AND STUDENT CHARACTERISTICS Detailed analysis of school characteristics and performance data. Seeking Accreditation Seeking Accreditation An institution that seeks accreditation confirms its commitment to educational quality. Learn More SEARCH ACCREDITED SCHOOLS Search our complete directory of ACCSC\naccredited vocational programs by school name, location, credentials and/or categories. THE STANDARDS OF ACCREDITATION The ACCSC hallmarks of quality by which post-secondary career schools are evaluated. INITIAL ACCREDITATION ELIGIBILITY The eligibility requirements and first steps of the accreditation process. RENEWAL OF ACCREDITATION The documentation necessary, including required exhibits and listing of substantive changes, to renew ACCSC accreditation. APPLICATION PROCESS Frequently asked questions and an overview of the application process, beginning with the Pre-Workshop Application for Initial Applicant Schools. Student Center Student Center ACCSC has established a comprehensive oversight system that ensures quality at our accredited member institutions in a number of different ways. Learn More Search Accredited Schools Search our complete directory of ACCSC\naccredited vocational programs by school name, location, credentials and/or categories. Prospective Students When you attend an ACCSC-accredited institution, you are attending a school that has undergone a rigorous process that evaluates educational quality. Transfer of Credit Accredited institutions should establish fair and equitable transfer of credit policies. Complaints The Commission's primary responsibility in reviewing complaints is to ensure that member schools remain in continuous compliance with accreditation requirements. Closed School Guide Information for students if the school they are attending will be closing. mikeroweWORKS Foundation The mikeroweWORKS Foundation Work Ethic Scholarship Program. Events and Recognition Events and Recognition Innovative, exciting and engaging activities are happening every day at ACCSC-accredited schools. We seek to recognize the outstanding work and efforts of our students, faculty and schools, and welcome you to join us as we work together toward our goal of ensuring quality education that enhances student success in the workforce. Learn More Award Winners The Commission celebrates the achievements and contributions of outstanding individuals and accredited schools each year, honoring them at the Professional Development Conference. Spotlight on Excellence Highlighting innovation and best practices at ACCSC accredited schools that better support today's students. Events ACCSC events are designed to give our member schools an opportunity to collaborate on developing and implementing effective, practical strategies to ensure efficiency in operations and enhance students' educational experience. Forms and Reports Forms and Reports The purpose of this section is to set forth the applications, reports, forms, and exhibits that ACCSC-accredited institutions must submit to the Commission as part of the accreditation process. Learn More School Submission Center The centralized platform to submit reports, forms, responses and other required information. Application Process Frequently asked questions and an overview of the application process, beginning with the Pre-Workshop Application for Initial Applicant Schools. Annual Report The electronic submission of the ACCSC Annual Report is required for all ACCSC-accredited institutions. Training and Resources Training and Resources Going through the rigorous process of accreditation requires a high level of engagement, knowledge and effort on the part of faculty, staft, and administrators.\nACCSC offers a variety of opportunities for training and professional development as well as other resources that will help build the necessary knowledge and skill sets for schools. Learn More Webinars Hear updates on recent ACCSC initiatives, as well as professional development opportunities for a variety of roles at high performing institutions. Administrators Faculty Development Administrators Faculty Development Resources Discover a variety of ACCSC resources designed to support accredited institutions in enhancing educational quality, ensuring consistency in operations, and promoting institutional improvement. Tutorials Monograph Blueprints School Submission Center New Student, Graduate, Employer Letters Employment Verification ACCSC Logo Tutorials Monograph Blueprints School Submission Center New Student, Graduate, Employer Letters Employment Verification ACCSC Logo Online Training Center Access the ACCSC Online Training Center to view and enroll in training opportunities. CAP Learn more about the ACCSC Certified Accreditation Professional Program. EWS Find out about the Essential Workforce Skills Programmatic Certification. Volunteers Volunteers ACCSC's Community of Volunteers support and enhance the Commission's work in a variety of ways through their active involvement in the accreditation process. Learn More Become a Volunteer One of the defining characteristics of ACCSC accreditation is the involvement by a community of volunteers who support and enhance the accreditation process. The Volunteer Zone We celebrate the contributions of our volunteers and recognize the impact they make here in the Volunteer Zone! Volunteer Training We welcome you to apply for a volunteer position. Upon approval, we'll provide all of the information you need about the training process and schedule. Online Training Center Access the ACCSC Online Training Center to view and enroll in training opportunities. Actions and Announcements Actions and Announcements It is the policy of ACCSC to provide written notice of its accrediting decisions in accordance with federal regulations. This includes providing notice to the U.S. Department of Education, appropriate State licensing or authorizing agencies, appropriate accrediting agencies, and the general public. Learn More Schools to be Considered The Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges (ACCSC) has prepared and published a list of the schools that may be considered at its next Commission meeting. Public Notice of Commission Action Latest public notices of ACCSC's accreditation decisions. Announcements Important information and announcements regarding Commission activities and initiatives. Warnings Actions taken when ACCSC has reason to believe an institution is not or may not be in compliance with accrediting standards. Probation Actions taken when ACCSC determines an institution is not in compliance with accrediting standards. SHOW CAUSE ORDER Actions taken when ACCSC determines an institution is not in compliance with accrediting standards. WITHDRAWAL / DENIAL ACTIONS Information about the actions taken by ACCSC to withdraw or deny accreditation of an institution. Voluntary Withdrawals / School Closures Schools that have voluntarily withdrawn from ACCSC accreditation or have ceased to operate. Call for Comments An invitation to review and comment on proposed changes to ACCSC's standards and policies. Accreditation Alerts Official notice regarding final adoption and promulgation of revisions to, or, interpretive guidance pertaining to, ACCSC's Rules and Standards. Ensuring Quality Education that Enhances Student Success in the Workforce Student Center Join the Community Initial Accreditation Eligibility Achieve Excellence Forms and Reports Continuous Quality Resources Skill up Response to Executive Order on Accreditation Learn More › Message from the Chair and Call for Nominations Learn More › October 1, 2025 Accreditation Alert Learn More › CHEA Board of Directors Awards Initial Recognition to ACCSC Learn More › Call for Nominations – ACCSC Nominating Committee Learn More › Upcoming Events More Events Sep 16 2026 Professional Development Conference (PDC) The PDC provides the one-of-a-kind opportunity to explore meaningful ways to enhance and promote student excellence within our schools and our communities through an educational program building on our shared commitment to supporting exceptional students and fostering a community dedicated to their success. The educational program is the heart of the PDC experience, featuring sessions presented by leaders from ACCSC’s Community of Partners in Education. At the PDC you’ll have tons of opportunity to make meaningful connections with ACCSC, school representatives, and our partner organizations. The PDC also gives us the chance to celebrate ACCSC-accredited schools for their exceptional commitment to students. Join us for three days of learning and connection! Learn More Oct 20 Accreditation Renewal Workshop – October 2026 The Accreditation Workshop provides an opportunity for participants to gain a better understanding of the Commission’s standards and procedures, as well as to share experiences with other schools in the accreditation process. Learn More Dec 07 Initial Accreditation Workshop – December 2026 The Pre-Workshop Application for Initial Applicant Schools is the first step for any institution seeking initial accreditation from ACCSC. Learn More Latest News More News Aug 26 Guidance for Flight Schools – Flight Instructor Qualifications Read More Read Announcement August 24, 2026 Nominating Committee Election Read Announcement July 7, 2026 Call for Commissioner Nominations Read Announcement Stay Connected Be informed with the latest ACCSC news and Happenings Keep me Connected! Privacy Policy Sitemap Complaints Contact Us Privacy Policy Sitemap Complaints Contact Us Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges 2101 Wilson Boulevard Suite 302 Arlington, Virginia 22201 (703) 247-4212 Main (703) 247-4533 Fax Facebook-f Linkedin-in Privacy Policy Sitemap Complaints Contact Us Privacy Policy Sitemap Complaints Contact Us © 2026 Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges Search Search Stay Connected Tell us a little about yourself. Name (Required) First Last Email (Required) Are You A... School Seeking Accreditation Student Seeking Education Institutions School administrator interested in training and events School administrator interested in accreditation policy Regulatory Partner Keep Me Connected!"
    }
  },
